            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A knit sock (100) comprising: a collar (110) having a perimeter edge (111) around an opening (112) for receiving a wearer's foot; a leg portion (114) extending from the collar (110); a foot portion (144) extending from the leg portion (114) and terminating at a toe end (146); and a heel portion (130) positioned between the leg portion (114) and the foot portion (144), the heel portion (130) having an Achilles section (132) and a plantar section (134); wherein: at least the Achilles section (132) comprises a knit structure having an alternating pattern comprising a first number of knit courses (136) knit with terry loops and a second number of knit courses (138) knit without terry loops; the plantar section (134) includes a first plurality of integrally knit grip strips (140) that extend from a lateral side to a medial side of the plantar section (134); and the first plurality of integrally knit grip strips (140) comprises terry loops.</p>
            </abstract>
